(area "intent" :when "the agent shows the user what it does now, a todo list, progress through items, or a question with fixed choices")

(memory "internal/intent/doing" :when "the agent is about to make an outward call: an mcp tool, the web or an llm"
  "(intent/doing \"text\") sets intent line, before every outward call: mcp tool, web, llm. Replaces line before. User sees each update live while step runs.")

(memory "internal/intent/todo" :when "work takes more than one step, a todo item just finished, or the plan changed"
  "- (intent/todo \"label\" ...) sets todo list, every item open. Work of more than one step: intent/todo first. Label kept from list before keeps its done mark.
- (intent/check \"label\") marks one todo done. Next form after the work form, same block, same step: never a later step or the final answer. Unknown label fails and names open ones.
  Code checks each item, never memory. Work returns, item done at once. Work raises: check never runs, item stays open. Promise work: await before check.
- Plan changed: edit list, keep it true. (intent/drop \"label\") removes one todo. (intent/move \"label\" position) moves it, 0 first, past the end puts it last. (intent/clear) empties list. Unknown label fails and names open ones.

(intent/todo \"sum scores\" \"average\")
(let ((scores '(3 9 4)))
  (let ((total (apply + scores)))
    (intent/check \"sum scores\")
    (let ((mean (/ total (length scores))))
      (intent/check \"average\")
      (list total mean))))")

(memory "internal/intent/progress" :when "the agent loops over items and knows how many steps the loop takes"
  "(intent/progress done total [ \"label\" ]) progress bar, done of total, inside the loop, each item. Integers, total at least 1, done at most total. Independent of todo. Known step count: intent/progress. Named steps: intent/todo.

(let ((i 0) (n 3))
  (dolist (issue '(\"a\" \"b\" \"c\"))
    (setq i (+ i 1))
    (intent/progress i n \"issues\")))")

(memory "internal/intent/ask" :when "the agent needs the user to pick between fixed choices before it goes on"
  "(intent/ask \"prompt\" '(\"A\" \"B\") [:multi t]) closed question, one pick; :multi t allows several. Closed choice for user: intent/ask, never question in prose. Ends turn after this step. Answer arrives as next message.

(intent/ask \"Which board?\" '(\"Sales\" \"Support\"))")
